# Lessons Learned

## What Worked
- Sysmon provided detailed process-creation telemetry.
- PowerShell Script Block Logging provided command visibility.
- Splunk enabled centralized investigation across multiple hosts.
- Detection documentation accelerated event searches.
- Group Policy maintained consistent endpoint protections.

## Challenges
- Raw XML fields required custom SPL extraction.
- Some Windows Security events depended on audit-policy coverage.
- Time-zone differences required careful timeline validation.
- VM resource constraints occasionally affected networking and ingestion.

## Improvements
- Improve field extraction for Windows and Sysmon events.
- Create scheduled alerts for account creation and privilege changes.
- Add dashboard panels for incident timelines.
- Establish consistent time synchronization checks.
- Expand incident-response testing with additional controlled scenarios.
